{#
    One glyph with no tile, as the app's own chrome wears it: the top bar's
    logo, and the pl mark's tab icon.

    The box is the 48 grid every glyph was drawn on, the one the pl mark's
    macro draws in too, so any icon here stands at the mark's scale. A glyph
    that needs its ground never comes here (LogoMotif::needsGround()).

    Variables (see BrandingController::bare()):
      motif       LogoMotif — which glyph template to draw
      p           the paints by part: '#rrggbb', 'url(#g)' or null
      glyph_ramp  seven stops when a part is a sweep, else null

    The gradient runs corner to corner across the glyph, (8,6) to (40,42), the
    same as on the tile, so a sweep reads the same with or without one.
#}
<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 48 48" width="48" height="48">
{% if glyph_ramp %}
    <defs>
        <linearGradient id="g" gradientUnits="userSpaceOnUse" x1="8" y1="6" x2="40" y2="42">
            {%- for stop in glyph_ramp %}<stop offset="{{ '%.3f'|format(loop.index0 / 6) }}" stop-color="{{ stop }}"/>{% endfor -%}
        </linearGradient>
    </defs>
{% endif %}
    {% include 'branding/motif/' ~ motif.value ~ '.svg.twig' with { p: p } only %}
</svg>
